RandGaussZiggurat: uniform random numbers in double precision (ATLAS's fork of CLHEP, commit
1085f1cc, ATR-26831). ziggurat_UNI() returned the engine's flat() as a float, which rounds
values just below 1.0 up to 1.0: ziggurat_nfix() then takes log(1.0 - 1.0), a division by zero
(and invalid operations after it), and draws a different number of random numbers than with
the exact value, which changes the random sequence of everything that shares the engine (e.g.
Geant4's, in ATLAS's simulation of transition radiation in the TRT).

--- a/Random/Random/RandGaussZiggurat.h	2026-10-11 20:44:23
+++ b/Random/Random/RandGaussZiggurat.h	2026-10-11 20:44:23
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
   static CLHEP_THREAD_LOCAL bool ziggurat_is_init;
   
   static inline unsigned long ziggurat_SHR3(HepRandomEngine* anEngine) {return (unsigned int)(*anEngine);};
-  static inline float ziggurat_UNI(HepRandomEngine* anEngine) {return anEngine->flat();};
+  static inline double ziggurat_UNI(HepRandomEngine* anEngine) {return anEngine->flat();};
   static inline float ziggurat_RNOR(HepRandomEngine* anEngine) {
     if(!ziggurat_is_init) ziggurat_init();
     long hz=(signed)ziggurat_SHR3(anEngine);
